# Project: Ethnic Wear E-commerce (prototype, ~70-80% prod-ready, config-driven)

## Stack (do not deviate without being asked)
- Backend: Django (latest LTS). NOT Flask.
- Frontend: Django templates + HTMX + Tailwind CSS + Alpine.js. Monolith, no separate SPA.
- DB: PostgreSQL in prod, SQLite for local dev only.
- Admin theme: django-unfold.
- Payments: Razorpay Standard Checkout.
- Invoices: WeasyPrint (HTML -> PDF).
- Shipping: Shiprocket API (optional, behind a toggle).
- CRM: Zoho CRM (optional) with a local Excel/CSV fallback.

## Core design principle: config over code
- All client-specific behavior lives in a single `StoreSettings` model editable from Django admin.
- Every integration (Razorpay, Shiprocket, Zoho) sits behind a small interface with a working
  fallback (e.g. Zoho off -> write invoice row to Excel; Shiprocket off -> manual status in admin).
- A half-configured store must still complete an order end-to-end.

## Data rules
- Sizes and colours are DATABASE ROWS, never hardcoded enums. Support 8+ colours, no hard cap.
- ProductVariant = product x size x colour, unique together, with its own SKU + stock.
- OrderItem snapshots price + tax at purchase time; never recompute from live product prices.

## Security (non-negotiable)
- NEVER store raw card/UPI data. Razorpay holds it.
- Payment truth = server-side webhook + signature verification. Never trust the browser's
  success callback to mark an order paid.
- All secrets (API keys, Zoho/Razorpay/Shiprocket creds) come from environment variables. No secrets in code or repo.
- Keep CSRF on. Rate-limit checkout endpoints. Validate pincode + phone on address input.

## GST
- GST logic is gated by `StoreSettings.gst_enabled`. When on: compute CGST/SGST/IGST, show GSTIN + HSN
  on the invoice. When off: plain invoice. Products carry optional hsn_code + gst_rate.

## Code conventions
- Python: type hints, docstrings on public functions, PEP 8, black formatting.
- Apps split by domain: catalog, cart, orders, payments, shipping, invoicing, accounts, core(settings).
- Business logic in services.py, not in views or models.
- Write a happy-path test for each critical flow: add-to-cart, checkout, payment webhook, invoice gen.
- Use Django migrations; never edit the DB by hand.
- HTMX for partial updates (cart, filters); Alpine for small client-side interactions only.

## Out of scope for v1 (do not build unless asked)
Coupons, wishlist, reviews, analytics dashboards, multi-currency, multi-vendor, loyalty.
